  "body": "What happens: a document with no mounted machine posts with the default machine file (`assets/machines/3axis-vmc.mch`). The post reads the name and the coolant words from that file. The program gate does not read its limits. The gate reads `Option<Machine>` from the mount, and that value is `None` when no machine is mounted.\n\nEvidence (review of PR #2320): a default machine file with a spindle maximum of zero and rapid speeds of zero posts with exit 0. The shipped file has a spindle maximum of 12000 rpm. An operation at a higher speed in a document with no mount posts with no refusal.\n\nExpected: the post judges a document with no mount against the same machine values that it posts with. Alternatively, the post says in the program report that no machine limits were checked.\n\nPriority: P3. The output can be wrong, but the user did not declare a machine. The workaround is to mount a machine on the setup. This gap is older than #2319.\n\nFound while fixing #2319.\n\nDone means: a document with no mounted machine is judged against the default machine's limits (or the report names the gap), with a pinning test.\n",
